  "summary": "作者释马头带剑：午对应马、擎羊喻剑；天同太阴午命的丙或戊生人有羊入命且会多吉时，可制煞为用，增斗志与开拓能力。古注丙禄权、戊权双禄夹分支保留，化曜未明不补星。刀剑比喻与古代武职论不作现实暴力断语。",
  "summary_en": "The source explains Ma Tou Dai Jian, Sword at the Horse’s Head: Wu corresponds to the horse and Qing Yang is likened to a sword. For Tian Tong and Tai Yin in Wu Life, Bing or Wu births with Qing Yang and many benefics may redirect malefic force into determination and outward expansion. The quoted Bing Lu/Quan and Wu Quan/double-Lu branches are retained without inventing unnamed transforming stars. Sword imagery and historical military interpretations are not predictions of real-world violence.",
